# NURTW Membership and Vehicle Verification System
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must stay that way.
# Never commit real credentials, and never paste them into documents or plans.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API (apps/api) — deployed to DigitalOcean
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3001

# Comma-separated browser origins permitted to call the API.
# Leave empty in production if the web application is served same-origin.
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — REQUIRED. The API refuses to start without it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development: `docker compose up -d` starts PostgreSQL 17 on port 5433.
# Port 5433, not the default 5432, because 5432 is occupied by an unrelated
# stack on the maintainer's machine — a shared default port is how two projects
# end up silently writing to one another's database.

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://nurtw:nurtw_local_dev@localhost:5433/nurtw?schema=public

# Production is Neon, EU region:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/db?sslmode=require
#
# ARCHITECTURE.md Decision 10.4: production data resides in an EU region
# (London or Frankfurt). Storing Nigerian members' personal data outside Nigeria
# is a cross-border transfer under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023; the
# Union's lawful basis for it is outstanding and due before go-live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Initial administrator — optional, roadmap item 03
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The seed creates a super administrator ONLY when both are supplied. There is
# deliberately no default password: a known credential in a seed script reaches
# production far more often than anyone expects, and this account holds
# vehicle.declare and every other permission in the catalogue.
#
# Set them for one run, create the account, then remove them.

# SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# SEED_ADMIN_NAME=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uploaded media — roadmap item 05
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ARCHITECTURE.md Decision 10.2: photographs and signatures live in object
# storage, never in the database and never in the repository. In development they
# are written to the filesystem; the directory is gitignored, because a member's
# passport photograph committed to history cannot be undone by deleting the file.

MEDIA_STORAGE_DIR=var/media

# Signs the time-limited links that serve uploaded files. Unset, a value is
# generated at start-up, which invalidates outstanding links on restart —
# acceptable in development, not in production, where two instances would sign
# differently and links minted by one would be refused by the other.

# MEDIA_URL_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sticker QR signing — from roadmap item 08
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRD §26, Requirement 26.2: the signing secret is held only by the issuing and
# verification services. It must never reach the web application, a QR payload,
# client-delivered code, or any log. The key id travels in the payload so the
# secret can be rotated without invalidating stickers already issued.

# STICKER_SIGNING_KEY_ID=k1
# STICKER_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Multi-factor sign-in — from roadmap item 28
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRD Requirement 17.1. Encrypts each officer's authenticator secret at rest,
# so a leaked database backup yields no working second factor. Use a long
# random value, held only by the API. Without it, setting up an authenticator
# answers 503.
#
# Changing it makes every stored secret unreadable: every officer must then
# set up their authenticator again. Do not rotate it casually.

# MFA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Members' NINs — from roadmap item 44
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRD Requirement 7.4. Seals each member's National Identification Number at
# rest, and keys the hash that keeps one NIN to one member's record. Use a
# long random value, held only by the API. Without it, recording a NIN
# answers 503; the rest of registering still works.
#
# Never change it once NINs are recorded: every one would become unreadable,
# and none could be matched again.

# IDENTITY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payments (Paystack) — from roadmap item 16
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRD Requirement 27.10: the secret key is held only by the API. It never
# appears in the web application, a log, an error message, or a URL. Use a
# test key (sk_test_...) everywhere except production.

# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=
# PAYSTACK_BASE_URL=https://api.paystack.co

# The bank Paystack opens members' dedicated accounts with (item 23). In test
# mode Paystack accepts only `test-bank`. In live mode use a provider slug from
# GET /dedicated_account/available_providers, e.g. `wema-bank` or
# `titan-paystack`. Unset, Paystack chooses.

# PAYSTACK_DVA_PREFERRED_BANK=test-bank

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Text messages (Termii) — from roadmap item 45
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRD Requirement 27.14 (revision 1.18): each payment is confirmed to the
# member by SMS. The API key sends; the base URL is the account's own, shown
# on Termii's dashboard; the secret key signs delivery reports. Held only by
# the API, never logged. Without the first two, nothing is sent and messages
# cannot be switched on in settings.

# TERMII_API_KEY=
# TERMII_BASE_URL=
# TERMII_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Who is calling — from roadmap item 55
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The address every limit, log, and audit event records. EDGE_PROXY names the
# proxy in front of the host's router: `cloudflare` on DigitalOcean App
# Platform. Unset trusts the router alone.
#
# WEB_FORWARDING_SECRET is shared with the website's server: with it, the
# website names each visitor's address to the API. Set the same value on
# both, never as NEXT_PUBLIC_. At least 32 characters. Never logged.

# EDGE_PROXY=cloudflare
# WEB_FORWARDING_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web (apps/web) — deployed to Vercel
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is exposed to the browser. Put nothing sensitive behind it.

# REQUIRED. Set it in apps/web/.env.local for local development.
#
# The web application throws on start-up in production when this is absent,
# rather than defaulting: a deployed build quietly pointing at localhost would
# appear to work in review and fail for every real user. Include the /api/v1
# prefix.

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/v1

# Server-only, read by src/proxy.ts at run time (item 55): the API's
# WEB_FORWARDING_SECRET. Set it only on Vercel, which writes the visitor's
# address itself; elsewhere a browser could name any address it liked.

# WEB_FORWARDING_SECRET=
